1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,840
This human may have been scared for her life, but we can take her word alone.

2
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:11,080
Let me borrow five soldiers, and I'll go see what's happening at City Hall, just in case.

3
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:15,380
That's not a bad idea. We'll regroup when you're done.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,200
That story protected you. Maybe you were his comrade.

5
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,720
No. You probably just used him like all the others do.

6
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,340
Okay, follow me. Let's see what's going on at City Hall.

7
00:00:53,340 --> 00:01:00,480
I'm coming, old friend.

8
00:01:03,620 --> 00:01:05,220
Is there something wrong?

9
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:08,800
No. It's just getting really cloudy.

10
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:11,600
It's the perfect weather to launch an attack.

11
00:01:12,980 --> 00:01:14,340
Yeah. Let's...

12
00:02:44,039 --> 00:03:14,019
I'll see you next time.

13
00:03:14,959 --> 00:03:19,039
Well, the vampires are definitely planning to ambush us.

14
00:03:19,279 --> 00:03:21,459
I'll have to reconsider what we should do next.

15
00:03:22,079 --> 00:03:23,419
What are you talking about?

16
00:03:24,019 --> 00:03:26,679
I mean, we're gonna go and rescue them, aren't we?

17
00:03:26,999 --> 00:03:30,079
So you're suggesting we walk head-on into something we know is a trap?

18
00:03:30,219 --> 00:03:31,799
Yeah, if we have to.

19
00:03:32,099 --> 00:03:33,139
Everyone shut up.

20
00:03:36,079 --> 00:03:36,519
Okay.

21
00:03:38,199 --> 00:03:41,679
We'll snipe and see how they react, just to test the waters.

22
00:03:41,679 --> 00:03:44,059
There are three targets inside.

23
00:03:44,199 --> 00:03:48,299
Powerful nobles named Crowley Eusford, Chess Bell, and Horned Skulled.

24
00:03:49,499 --> 00:03:54,239
If it looks like our enemies are too strong for us to defeat, we'll leave the hostages.

25
00:03:54,919 --> 00:03:56,439
What? Give up?

26
00:03:56,899 --> 00:03:59,259
There's no way I'm leaving them hanging there like that.

27
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:01,099
Hey, you've gotta calm down.

28
00:04:01,619 --> 00:04:05,239
Lieutenant Colonel, what do you believe is our top priority at this point in the mission?

29
00:04:05,599 --> 00:04:08,639
We can't afford to lose any more troops, especially elites like you.

30
00:04:09,019 --> 00:04:11,979
That makes freeing the hostages a secondary concern.

31
00:04:12,519 --> 00:04:14,359
Moving forward, I'm gonna need all of you.

32
00:04:14,359 --> 00:04:18,939
What you're saying is, this isn't over.

33
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:22,519
We have to survive because there's another mission waiting after this one, right?

34
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:24,939
Well, that's one way to look at it.

35
00:04:25,199 --> 00:04:27,099
We need to keep the vampires in Nagaya.

36
00:04:27,739 --> 00:04:30,519
Doing so lets our main unit in Shibuya move undetected.

37
00:04:31,199 --> 00:04:33,279
That's one of the primary reasons we're here.

38
00:04:33,559 --> 00:04:36,059
Wait, so the Shibuya team is on the move right now?

39
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:40,559
Yeah. If things are going as planned, they should be on their way to Shinjuku.

40
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:45,979
So basically, what he's saying is that this whole attack on Nagaya was nothing but a decoy.

41
00:04:46,219 --> 00:04:46,899
Not exactly.

42
00:04:47,339 --> 00:04:50,259
The extermination of the nobles will have a huge impact on the war.

43
00:04:50,919 --> 00:04:55,439
But from now on, our mission is to keep the enemy distracted as long as we possibly can.

44
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:56,799
Which is why...

45
00:04:56,799 --> 00:04:59,679
We're gonna see how they react to a little expert snipey.

46
00:05:00,059 --> 00:05:01,759
If they attack in force, we'll run.

47
00:05:02,319 --> 00:05:05,659
But if we see an opening, we'll try to save all of the hostages.

48
00:05:06,059 --> 00:05:08,879
Best-case scenario, we'll kill the nobles too.

49
00:05:09,079 --> 00:05:11,799
Now you're dreaming. Things never go that well.

50
00:05:13,379 --> 00:05:15,379
Why are you always such a pessimist?

51
00:05:16,139 --> 00:05:18,619
Come on, Curran, I'm just telling it like it is.

52
00:05:18,819 --> 00:05:20,759
Don't worry, I'm still gonna kill these guys.

53
00:05:22,359 --> 00:05:24,039
Pick a sniping perch, Yoichi.

54
00:05:24,539 --> 00:05:26,159
Let's show everyone what you've learned.

55
00:05:26,199 --> 00:05:26,439
Right.

56
00:05:28,819 --> 00:05:30,579
Look alive and get into position.

57
00:05:30,859 --> 00:05:32,579
Be ready for a swift counterattack.

58
00:05:32,759 --> 00:05:33,339
Roger that.

59
00:05:34,259 --> 00:05:35,619
We're prepared, right?

60
00:05:36,059 --> 00:05:36,579
Yeah.

61
00:05:38,879 --> 00:05:40,699
Okay, I've got the fourth floor.

62
00:05:41,079 --> 00:05:43,639
Focus your attention on the windows in the next level up.

63
00:05:43,799 --> 00:05:44,219
Got it.

64
00:05:44,219 --> 00:05:56,519
Hey, I've got a visual on a vampire.

65
00:05:57,119 --> 00:05:57,839
It's a noble.

66
00:05:58,339 --> 00:05:59,139
His back's to me.

67
00:05:59,439 --> 00:06:00,759
I don't think he's noticed us yet.

68
00:06:00,999 --> 00:06:02,079
Then take the damn shot.

69
00:06:02,339 --> 00:06:02,739
Now!

70
00:06:03,459 --> 00:06:05,079
Fly true for me, Gekko-een.

71
00:06:05,079 --> 00:06:20,459
What is this thing?

72
00:06:20,459 --> 00:06:20,499
What is this thing?

73
00:06:22,359 --> 00:06:23,499
How strange.

74
00:06:23,499 --> 00:06:36,859
Sir, I failed to hit my target.

75
00:06:36,859 --> 00:06:40,719
Ordinarily, even a noble wouldn't have been able to dodge a shot like that.

76
00:06:41,019 --> 00:06:42,179
Which means...

77
00:06:42,179 --> 00:06:44,739
That this guy must be an extremely powerful vampire.

78
00:06:45,439 --> 00:06:48,319
It's no wonder nine of our strongest teams couldn't handle him.

79
00:06:48,599 --> 00:06:49,679
We don't stand a chance.

80
00:06:50,639 --> 00:06:51,319
He's right.

81
00:06:51,319 --> 00:06:53,239
I recognize this guy.

82
00:06:53,339 --> 00:06:54,339
We faced him before.

83
00:06:54,559 --> 00:06:54,839
Huh?

84
00:06:55,059 --> 00:06:57,579
He's the vampire we fought when we were headed to Shinjuku.

85
00:06:58,059 --> 00:06:59,499
And his comrades are with him.

86
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:00,299
Huh?

87
00:07:00,299 --> 00:07:11,119
Hey, give me that!

88
00:07:12,699 --> 00:07:14,439
Are you okay, Lord Crowley?

89
00:07:14,619 --> 00:07:15,979
What was that weird thing?

90
00:07:16,099 --> 00:07:17,599
Some kind of exploding bird?

91
00:07:17,959 --> 00:07:20,039
It would appear that we have some visitors.

92
00:07:24,839 --> 00:07:25,579
Yoichi's right.

93
00:07:25,939 --> 00:07:27,139
That guy is big trouble.

94
00:07:27,399 --> 00:07:28,739
He's like insanely strong.

95
00:07:29,159 --> 00:07:29,819
I see.

96
00:07:29,819 --> 00:07:32,579
Then I highly doubt we could beat him by force alone.

97
00:07:33,019 --> 00:07:34,259
So then, what?

98
00:07:34,759 --> 00:07:36,059
We've got two choices.

99
00:07:37,459 --> 00:07:40,299
We can shoot our comrades now before they're tortured.

100
00:07:40,539 --> 00:07:42,359
And then get the hell out of this town.

101
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,559
You can't be serious!

102
00:07:44,699 --> 00:07:46,119
Hey, don't freak out yet!

103
00:07:46,959 --> 00:07:49,079
That's one way, but what's the other option?

104
00:07:49,619 --> 00:07:53,719
We somehow managed to split up the nobles, then save the hostages and retreat.

105
00:07:54,719 --> 00:07:56,679
Naturally, that plan's more dangerous.

106
00:07:57,319 --> 00:07:58,799
I doubt we'd all survive.

107
00:07:58,799 --> 00:08:04,659
We're not leaving our comrades behind, right?

108
00:08:04,919 --> 00:08:05,279
Gorin?

109
00:08:05,279 --> 00:08:14,879
I think the smartest move is to kill the hostages and run.

110
00:08:15,359 --> 00:08:17,639
They didn't attack us after Yoichi's failed shot.

111
00:08:18,199 --> 00:08:19,679
So we're not important to them.

112
00:08:19,919 --> 00:08:21,619
We should retreat while we're still able to.

113
00:08:21,619 --> 00:08:22,999
You bastard!

114
00:08:22,999 --> 00:08:23,019
You bastard!

115
00:08:23,559 --> 00:08:24,599
Don't be stupid!

116
00:08:24,799 --> 00:08:26,199
You're the one who's acting stupid!

117
00:08:26,199 --> 00:08:30,079
I've got close friends in that group of hostages.

118
00:08:30,559 --> 00:08:32,999
It's killing me to even think of leaving them behind.

119
00:08:33,559 --> 00:08:36,039
But you don't see me making a scene like a spoiled brat.

120
00:08:36,039 --> 00:08:42,399
But, Lieutenant Colonel, this is still a decoy mission, isn't it?

121
00:08:42,659 --> 00:08:46,199
If we leave the nobles alone, aren't we putting the Shibuya unit at risk?

122
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:46,779
Yes.

123
00:08:47,299 --> 00:08:48,459
Well, in that case...

124
00:08:48,459 --> 00:08:49,079
Yeah, I know.

125
00:08:49,739 --> 00:08:50,899
There's no way around it.

126
00:08:50,939 --> 00:08:51,819
We have to attack.

127
00:08:52,419 --> 00:08:55,119
We'll put on a big show so they think we're the main unit.

128
00:08:55,459 --> 00:08:57,499
I'm not against killing the bloodsuckers.

129
00:08:57,499 --> 00:09:01,339
But I don't see how we stand a chance with them waiting around for us like this.

130
00:09:01,419 --> 00:09:03,539
If they start to overwhelm us, we'll retreat.

131
00:09:04,019 --> 00:09:04,419
Come on.

132
00:09:04,759 --> 00:09:05,979
We should move locations.

133
00:09:15,879 --> 00:09:16,779
How odd.

134
00:09:16,899 --> 00:09:17,979
There's no second wave.

135
00:09:18,419 --> 00:09:20,959
We could have some fun and go hunt them down ourselves.

136
00:09:21,279 --> 00:09:24,139
I would bet that's exactly what our enemies are hoping for.

137
00:09:24,479 --> 00:09:26,419
We'll be patient and let them come to us.

138
00:09:26,419 --> 00:09:31,159
They must have realized that they didn't stand a chance against us after their first attack failed.

139
00:09:31,319 --> 00:09:33,059
Maybe they just got scared and ran away.

140
00:09:33,639 --> 00:09:36,539
Humans have a bad habit of making stupid decisions,

141
00:09:36,779 --> 00:09:39,159
especially when the smart choice is against their orders.

142
00:09:39,699 --> 00:09:40,039
Huh?

143
00:09:40,419 --> 00:09:42,219
Wait, what do you mean, Lord Crowley?

144
00:09:42,419 --> 00:09:46,519
They've been commanded to destroy us, so there's little chance they're going to back out now.

145
00:09:47,039 --> 00:09:49,659
They're loyal even in the face of certain death.

146
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:51,819
Or there's something else.

147
00:09:53,019 --> 00:09:55,219
It's possible they have a hidden agenda.

148
00:09:56,419 --> 00:10:00,919
Farid's going to want to know everything about this attack.

149
00:10:01,159 --> 00:10:03,119
We should gather as much intel as possible.

150
00:10:03,919 --> 00:10:05,259
I don't like Lord Farid.

151
00:10:05,319 --> 00:10:06,979
He's always trying to seem so mysterious.

152
00:10:07,479 --> 00:10:08,099
It's annoying.

153
00:10:09,019 --> 00:10:11,759
You know, Chess, for once I actually agree with you.

154
00:10:12,159 --> 00:10:13,339
He can be a little much.

155
00:10:13,339 --> 00:10:16,599
But you have to admit, when he's around, there's never a dull moment.

156
00:10:19,399 --> 00:10:20,319
All right, ladies.

157
00:10:20,399 --> 00:10:21,639
Here's our new plan of attack.

158
00:10:21,959 --> 00:10:25,039
We capture the commander, since he's the one who will have the most info.

159
00:10:25,879 --> 00:10:26,439
Got it?

160
00:10:26,739 --> 00:10:27,139
Yes.

161
00:10:27,139 --> 00:10:35,559
Pay attention.

162
00:10:35,719 --> 00:10:36,619
Here's the new plan.

163
00:10:37,639 --> 00:10:41,019
Shinya and the rest of my team will attack Crowley, Usford, and his comrades.

164
00:10:41,839 --> 00:10:45,819
Shinya and Narumi's teams will attempt to rescue the hostages while we're fighting.

165
00:10:46,239 --> 00:10:48,259
Do you think you'll be all right with just you guys?

166
00:10:48,739 --> 00:10:51,139
Our basic strategy will be to strike and run away.

167
00:10:51,599 --> 00:10:53,299
We should be able to hold them off for a bit.

168
00:10:53,799 --> 00:10:57,339
That's only going to give you five minutes to rescue all the hostages you can.

169
00:10:57,699 --> 00:11:02,039
After that, we have to retreat and join the other teams at the Nagaya airport at once.

170
00:11:03,039 --> 00:11:04,999
Where are we going after we get to the airport?

171
00:11:04,999 --> 00:11:10,059
There should be a transport helicopter waiting for us there, along with new directives.

172
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:11,459
We'll follow those orders.

173
00:11:12,219 --> 00:11:13,999
We attack in seven minutes.

174
00:11:14,819 --> 00:11:16,479
Everyone, take your positions.

175
00:11:16,899 --> 00:11:17,459
Yes, sir.

176
00:11:24,839 --> 00:11:26,219
How does it look, Shinya?

177
00:11:26,719 --> 00:11:28,759
Our enemies aren't making any moves.

178
00:11:29,019 --> 00:11:31,339
But then, they're most likely waiting on us.

179
00:11:31,899 --> 00:11:33,319
Who knows what's inside, though?

180
00:11:33,319 --> 00:11:35,179
We're walking into this partially blind.

181
00:11:38,779 --> 00:11:41,519
Lieutenant Colonel, are we really attacking them first?

182
00:11:41,779 --> 00:11:42,099
Yeah.

183
00:11:42,839 --> 00:11:47,799
With Ghoshy's illusionary spell, he can make it look like 200 men are fighting alongside of us.

184
00:11:48,419 --> 00:11:49,539
Isn't that right?

185
00:11:50,059 --> 00:11:52,179
Sure, but there's one big problem with your plan.

186
00:11:52,599 --> 00:11:54,779
I'd have to get dangerously close to our enemies.

187
00:11:55,479 --> 00:11:57,079
Then why are you still standing here?

188
00:11:57,199 --> 00:11:57,359
What?

189
00:11:59,099 --> 00:12:01,459
Sounds like Ghoshy's our first casualty.

190
00:12:01,459 --> 00:12:03,319
Geez, thanks for the vote of confidence.

191
00:12:11,919 --> 00:12:13,379
Should we do this together?

192
00:12:13,959 --> 00:12:14,399
No.

193
00:12:14,659 --> 00:12:17,539
If we're going to free as many of them as we can in five minutes.

194
00:12:17,879 --> 00:12:19,119
Then we should go separately.

195
00:12:20,179 --> 00:12:20,559
Okay.

196
00:12:21,239 --> 00:12:22,059
Good luck to you.

197
00:12:22,319 --> 00:12:22,759
Thanks.

198
00:12:22,759 --> 00:12:24,519
Oh, yeah.

199
00:12:24,879 --> 00:12:26,259
And one more thing, noobs.

200
00:12:28,439 --> 00:12:29,719
Don't you dare die.

201
00:12:31,499 --> 00:12:32,919
Same goes for you guys.

202
00:12:34,099 --> 00:12:36,719
Oh, I'm not concerned about my squad surviving this.

203
00:12:36,979 --> 00:12:39,359
Not when they've got an incredible team leader like me.

204
00:12:42,859 --> 00:12:43,499
That's all.

205
00:12:43,899 --> 00:12:44,479
Let's move.

206
00:12:44,799 --> 00:12:46,179
We've got comrades to save.

207
00:12:46,519 --> 00:12:47,139
Roger that.

208
00:12:47,139 --> 00:12:49,799
We should move to our positions, too.

209
00:12:50,079 --> 00:12:50,379
Yeah.

210
00:12:54,759 --> 00:12:55,439
All right.

211
00:12:55,519 --> 00:12:57,099
There's no use putting this off.

212
00:13:00,139 --> 00:13:02,679
If you have any last words, now's your chance.

213
00:13:02,799 --> 00:13:03,299
We're ready.

214
00:13:03,739 --> 00:13:04,899
You can count on us.

215
00:13:04,899 --> 00:13:05,319
Okay.

216
00:13:05,319 --> 00:13:10,939
Okay, everyone.

217
00:13:11,079 --> 00:13:12,319
Let's synchronize our clocks.

218
00:13:13,059 --> 00:13:15,739
Please set an alarm for exactly five minutes.

219
00:13:16,419 --> 00:13:20,199
When it goes off, we have to retreat no matter what's happening at the time.

220
00:13:21,019 --> 00:13:22,259
Do you understand?

221
00:13:23,439 --> 00:13:24,559
This is an order.

222
00:13:24,939 --> 00:13:29,179
When our time is up, we leave the battlefield no matter how many people we've saved.

223
00:13:29,599 --> 00:13:31,419
That's the only rule for this mission.

224
00:13:31,899 --> 00:13:33,019
It can't be broken.

225
00:13:33,019 --> 00:13:37,539
That means, even if we have to leave someone behind, we retreat.

226
00:13:38,199 --> 00:13:38,759
But...

227
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:39,799
No buts, Yu.

228
00:13:40,179 --> 00:13:41,619
I'm the team leader here.

229
00:13:42,199 --> 00:13:43,679
We can only get out of this.

230
00:13:43,879 --> 00:13:45,779
But disobeying puts us all at risk.

231
00:13:46,259 --> 00:13:47,019
So please...

232
00:13:47,839 --> 00:13:49,639
Please follow my orders.

233
00:13:50,279 --> 00:13:51,279
Be a good soldier.

234
00:13:54,599 --> 00:13:55,319
I will.

235
00:13:57,019 --> 00:13:58,479
It's a simple job.

236
00:13:58,859 --> 00:14:00,659
All we have to do is save everyone.

237
00:14:00,659 --> 00:14:03,239
I don't think you get how hard this is going to be.

238
00:14:03,599 --> 00:14:03,899
No.

239
00:14:04,039 --> 00:14:05,439
I think this is going to work out.

240
00:14:05,839 --> 00:14:07,839
Our teamwork has gotten a lot better, too.

241
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:08,839
Hmm.

242
00:14:09,319 --> 00:14:12,299
And on top of that, we've all become really good friends.

243
00:14:12,799 --> 00:14:14,559
That might be an exaggeration.

244
00:14:15,299 --> 00:14:15,739
Hey.

245
00:14:16,439 --> 00:14:17,779
Why are you so mean?

246
00:14:18,699 --> 00:14:19,819
I'm just kidding.

247
00:14:19,819 --> 00:14:27,319
It's time to move out.

248
00:14:27,999 --> 00:14:28,419
Yeah.

249
00:14:28,419 --> 00:14:30,819
What do you think?

250
00:14:30,819 --> 00:15:00,799
I don't know.

251
00:15:00,819 --> 00:15:11,099
Lieutenant Colonel, what are you doing here?

252
00:15:11,219 --> 00:15:12,199
They're too powerful.

253
00:15:12,619 --> 00:15:15,279
You've got to get out of here. Just go on without us.

254
00:15:18,299 --> 00:15:19,519
Go get them.

255
00:15:19,859 --> 00:15:20,899
Damn, my cock.

256
00:15:21,539 --> 00:15:23,279
All right, do it, Ghoshy.

257
00:15:30,819 --> 00:15:35,879
Behold the Demon Army's best men. Let's do this.

258
00:15:35,959 --> 00:15:36,479
Attack!

259
00:15:40,979 --> 00:15:42,579
Don't let them into the building!

260
00:15:49,819 --> 00:15:53,259
Are they just going to leave us all hanging here?

261
00:15:53,259 --> 00:15:56,959
Are you okay?

262
00:15:57,079 --> 00:15:58,699
Narumi, what's going on?

263
00:15:59,119 --> 00:16:00,899
Kageyama, Yayoi, Rika.

264
00:16:01,679 --> 00:16:03,679
Get the other members of Kado's team free.

265
00:16:05,719 --> 00:16:07,259
Shusaku, you're coming with me.

266
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:15,359
There we go.

267
00:16:15,359 --> 00:16:17,139
Things are finally getting interesting.

268
00:16:23,999 --> 00:16:26,819
Huh. I've seen that face before.

269
00:16:27,359 --> 00:16:29,419
You must be leading this hopeless assault.

270
00:16:29,679 --> 00:16:31,739
I'm here to destroy you, blood sucker!

271
00:16:35,319 --> 00:16:37,099
It looks like you're pretty strong.

272
00:16:37,579 --> 00:16:38,899
But that's not enough!

273
00:16:38,899 --> 00:16:47,659
What about you, Commander?

274
00:16:48,179 --> 00:16:49,059
Rookie mistake.

275
00:16:49,419 --> 00:16:50,679
Not watching your back.

276
00:16:51,019 --> 00:16:53,159
Well, I guess this is checkmate.

277
00:17:04,159 --> 00:17:05,639
Lieutenant Colonel Curran!

278
00:17:05,639 --> 00:17:08,539
Leave it to them.

279
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,839
If we step in and try to help out,

280
00:17:10,919 --> 00:17:12,399
we'll only end up getting in the way.

281
00:17:12,619 --> 00:17:13,379
We have to!

282
00:17:14,679 --> 00:17:16,039
I've got a better idea.

283
00:17:17,039 --> 00:17:18,059
What are your orders?

284
00:17:19,139 --> 00:17:20,459
Continue the mission as planned.

285
00:17:21,119 --> 00:17:23,539
Move fast and save as many of the troops as you can.

286
00:17:24,419 --> 00:17:25,999
Shinoah, should we try and help them?

287
00:17:28,219 --> 00:17:30,159
Are we just going to let Goran die?

288
00:17:30,379 --> 00:17:32,159
Let's get up there and take out some nobles!

289
00:17:32,599 --> 00:17:33,639
Not a bad idea.

290
00:17:33,639 --> 00:17:36,199
You might be able to launch some kind of pincer attack.

291
00:17:36,479 --> 00:17:37,099
Yeah, Shinoah.

292
00:17:37,319 --> 00:17:38,119
Let's do it.

293
00:17:40,299 --> 00:17:40,739
Okay.

294
00:17:40,999 --> 00:17:42,159
We've got three minutes.

295
00:17:42,299 --> 00:17:43,779
Plenty of time to save the day.

296
00:17:44,319 --> 00:17:45,039
Let's go!

297
00:17:46,039 --> 00:17:47,819
I'll come up with a plan on the way.

298
00:17:48,619 --> 00:17:50,719
Please promise that you'll do as I say.

299
00:17:50,719 --> 00:18:02,259
Oh, that guy's going to be a problem.

300
00:18:03,139 --> 00:18:05,539
He's on a totally different level than the other nobles.

301
00:18:06,259 --> 00:18:08,239
I'm afraid this might be it for us.

302
00:18:09,459 --> 00:18:10,199
No way.

303
00:18:10,419 --> 00:18:11,939
Things are all going as I planned.

304
00:18:11,939 --> 00:18:14,539
Who are you trying to kid, Goran?

305
00:18:14,879 --> 00:18:17,319
At least we did a solid job of getting their attention.

306
00:18:17,959 --> 00:18:19,479
You and I make pretty good bait.

307
00:18:20,119 --> 00:18:20,879
You done rusting?

308
00:18:20,979 --> 00:18:22,619
Because I'd kind of like to escape now.

309
00:18:23,319 --> 00:18:24,259
You can't leave.

310
00:18:24,319 --> 00:18:25,719
The fun's just getting started.

311
00:18:25,719 --> 00:18:33,839
It'd be a shame for you two to miss the main event.

312
00:18:36,619 --> 00:18:38,259
I insist you stay.

313
00:18:38,399 --> 00:18:40,619
I can't allow you to disappoint Lord Grohler.

314
00:18:41,279 --> 00:18:43,599
Why can't we just start the show already?

315
00:18:43,999 --> 00:18:45,379
I'm feeling thirsty.

316
00:18:45,379 --> 00:18:47,859
I don't want to be rude.

317
00:18:48,079 --> 00:18:50,919
Then I guess we have to stay here and keep the three of them entertained.

318
00:18:58,659 --> 00:19:00,159
Why are you going that way?

319
00:19:01,019 --> 00:19:03,099
Goran and Shinya are on the fourth floor.

320
00:19:03,239 --> 00:19:05,219
Just stay quiet and follow my lead.

321
00:19:07,399 --> 00:19:08,159
You murdered.

322
00:19:15,379 --> 00:19:34,179
Lord Grohler, shall we join this dance?

323
00:19:34,179 --> 00:19:34,939
Don't worry.

324
00:19:35,059 --> 00:19:36,499
I can handle these two on my own.

325
00:19:37,079 --> 00:19:39,059
You shouldn't take your rice off of me!

326
00:19:42,119 --> 00:19:44,699
You're finally starting to put up a real fight.

327
00:19:45,379 --> 00:19:46,779
You're finally starting to put up a real fight.

328
00:19:49,779 --> 00:19:50,779
Why are you going to put up a real fight?

329
00:19:53,999 --> 00:19:54,719
Now!

330
00:20:02,539 --> 00:20:06,119
This is going to get boring if you keep repeating that same move.

331
00:20:09,119 --> 00:20:09,879
Oh.

332
00:20:11,719 --> 00:20:13,519
It appears that they've escaped.

333
00:20:15,379 --> 00:20:17,359
So how badly are you wounded, Shinya?

334
00:20:17,839 --> 00:20:18,839
It could be worse.

335
00:20:18,919 --> 00:20:20,479
I could have broken all my bones.

336
00:20:20,839 --> 00:20:22,939
If you're strong enough to choke, then walk on your own.

337
00:20:23,259 --> 00:20:24,879
You're not getting rid of me that easily.

338
00:20:25,439 --> 00:20:27,419
This way I can hold them off behind us.

339
00:20:29,999 --> 00:20:30,479
Hey!

340
00:20:30,919 --> 00:20:32,519
Why are you running away?

341
00:20:32,979 --> 00:20:34,979
To be honest, I've never really liked running.

342
00:20:35,539 --> 00:20:37,219
You could always stop chasing us!

343
00:20:37,219 --> 00:20:45,059
You guys attacked us first, and now you don't want us coming after you?

344
00:20:45,179 --> 00:20:47,819
I'm always amazed at how selfish humans can be.

345
00:20:50,939 --> 00:20:51,579
Are they coming?

346
00:20:52,959 --> 00:20:53,399
No.

347
00:20:54,599 --> 00:20:57,599
Maybe I managed to scare the bastards off with that last shot.

348
00:20:59,179 --> 00:20:59,879
Shinya!

349
00:20:59,879 --> 00:21:10,719
